{"id":"nc1e5f87577","headline":"RBI MPC Meeting 2026: Central bank flags a threat for Indian agriculture warming up in the Pacific","summary":"The Reserve Bank of India cut its FY27 inflation forecast to 5%, while flagging El Niño and an uneven southwest monsoon as risks to agriculture and rural demand. Governor Sanjay Malhotra cited volatile crude prices and geopolitical tensions.","why":"The RBI sets India's benchmark interest rates and inflation outlook, which influence bond yields, the rupee and corporate borrowing costs. Monsoon performance strongly affects India's farm output and inflation.","category":"economy","event_type":"rates","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Mumbai","country":"India","lat":19.08,"lon":72.88,"region":"asia"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/economy/agriculture/rbi-mpc-meeting-2026-central-bank-flags-a-threat-for-indian-agriculture-warming-up-in-the-pacific/articleshow/132892144.cms"},"sources":[{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/economy/agriculture/rbi-mpc-meeting-2026-central-bank-flags-a-threat-for-indian-agriculture-warming-up-in-the-pacific/articleshow/132892144.cms"}],"published_at":"2026-08-05T05:38:00Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-11T22:35:51Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"5327415e0d0ade3f","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-11T22:35:51Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-08-05T05:38:00Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-08-05T06:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"IR","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/bank-building-9545194.jpg","alt":"bank building (illustration)","credit":"Tho-Ge","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/